/E (        The Research Objectives section describes what your study intends to accomplish. It translates the research problem into clear, specific, and achievable goals. While the problem statement identifies what is wrong and the research questions ask what you want to find out, the objectives explain what you will do to find the answers. In other words, this section tells the reader the purpose, scope, and expected direction of your research. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
